  "title": "Enactivism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Francisco Varela, Evan Thompson and Eleanor Rosch hold that cognition is the sense-making of autonomous living systems, which bring forth a world of meaning through their own activity. Consciousness is a process of the living organism coupled to its world, not of the brain alone, and neurophenomenology studies it by joining trained first-person reports to measures of large-scale brain dynamics.",
